        'clinical_example' => "A hypothetical case involves a 26-year-old graphic designer who reports a three-year history of unpredictable mood swings. For weeks at a time, the designer sleeps 5 hours a night, takes on multiple freelance projects, and feels elevated and creative; then, without clear triggers, transitions into several weeks of feeling down, low in energy, and self-doubting.\n\nDetailed clinical assessment confirms that the elevated periods never meet the full 4-day threshold for a full hypomanic episode and cause no marked dysfunction, while the low periods never feature the 5 criteria required for a major depressive episode. The designer has never had more than four consecutive weeks of normal mood over the past three years. Meeting all criteria, the diagnosis is Cyclothymic Disorder.",
